Well, my latest attempt at an elvish wizard reached its end last night.  
He'd made it to Minetown, which turned out to be a bones from an earlier 
wizard (unfortunately, she'd died in a shop, so no immediately free 
stuff).  He rather quickly ran into the vampire bat which had been the 
demise of the first wizard; after his cat died, and he was getting rather 
beat up (he was still level 1), he slapped on his ring of poly control 
(initial equipment) and zapped his wand of poly at himself (found it two 
squares from the start).  The bat was unable to compete with the new 
vampire lord; things were starting to look up.

After playing around in town (and being reminded the hard way that bones 
piles tend to be cursed), he decided to head over to Sokoban.  He'd gained 
some experience by now, but was still using force bolt.  Went down a 
flight of stairs--hmm, three soldier ants.  Probably not a safe 
situation.  Re-polyed into another vampire lord, scared one ant, had to 
retreat because of the other two.  Back up stairs.  Wandered around a 
little more, found a cat, who quickly became a pet.  Decided cats are 
nice, but could be better, so he zapped it with his wand of poly (turned 
out to be the last charge), and got a mind flayer.  Decent, he thinks, and 
decides to head back down to see how his pal does against ants.

Forgot that, since I'd returned to elven (non-flying) form, I needed to 
check my load--I was burdenned.  Bad.  Went down the stairs, and didn't 
get a chance to do anything before the two ants right next to the stairs 
slaughtered me.  Ouch.  Left a bones, of course, but I'm not sure any 
character I take is going to be ready for it (mind flayer and four soldier 
ants by the stairs, on dlvl 7)...

Out of curiosity, what forms do people chose to poly into for fighting?  
Vampire Lords?  Archons?  Enquiring minds want to know!  :-)

